  "limits": [
    "Explicit offline synthetic power-on and acquisition-actuator inputs; no physical camera observation or accepted hardware-ready profile.",
    "Rear-panel SPI1 takes whole sixteen-bit words (first stock word 0x401); panel register meaning is unknown.",
    "Same canonical graph; status transitions depend only on completed wire commands, not firmware task RAM.",
    "ADC8 and ADC9 use released level1023; S1/S2 pins are static active-low inputs.",
    "Owner-captured X-M1 ROM and declared512MiB DRAM backing; unselected initial input values remain unmeasured.",
    "Explicit absent external-flash input atGPIO11/2=0 and fixed-low SPI0 MISO; existing bounded law, unmeasured external part/line.",
    "Declared acquisition actuator response: GPIO1 pins1/2 drive GPIO0 pin9 rising / pin6 falling through target EXR IRQ11; initial GPIO0 sensors high and GPIO2 pin8 low. Motion law, actuator identity and latency are unmeasured.",
    "Normal power-on status0x10 selects stock boot kind2 via6A5AAC/table7CB7AC; hardware-observed0x400a00c0 samples0x10/0x12 classify the same (E-DUMP-RAM-150). GPIO0.2=1 releases active-low S1. Status0 selected kind3, whose69CFA4 guard rejects released S1. MENU/OK ADC9=1023 releases its configured0..255 band. Pin and ADC levels are synthetic."
  ],
